OL,3,GNEWSAHome Guard training documents
OL,4,Adiscovered in attic
OL,5,
OL,6,FA set of documents showing how local
OL,7,FHome Guard volunteers were trained
OL,8,Fduring World War Two have been
OL,9,Fdiscovered in an attic.
OL,11,FThe typewritten pages show scenarios to
OL,12,Ftest how officers from E Company of the
OL,13,F4th (Forest of Dean) Battalion Home
OL,14,FGuard, based in Mitcheldean, would
OL,15,Frespond to different situations,
OL,16,Fincluding finding four dead Germans
OL,17,Flying near motor cycles at Westbury on
OL,18,FSevern.
OL,23,APub: 29-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
